=document :!auto-toc
=begin rakudoc
=TITLE Run the RakuDoc editor locally
=for AUTHOR :hidden
Richard Hainswotth, aka finanalyst

Since the full renderer to handle citations and various other plugins has some large dependencies, I have created 

The following is written assuming a Linux OS and so it should work with, eg.,  Ubuntu and Apple. 
I have not tested this with a MS system, and I would be happy to have comments to adapt the following.

Let's start. 

=numitem We need to have [podman](https://podman-desktop.io/) installed.   
=begin numitem
In a terminal
=begin code
podman pull docker.io/finanalyst/browser-editor:latest
podman run -d --name rakedit  --network=host --rm docker.io/finanalyst/rakudoc_browser:latest
=end code
For Mac users, try
=begin code
podman pull docker.io/finanalyst/browser-editor:latest
podman run -d  --name rakedit --platform linux/amd64 --rm docker.io/finanalyst/rakudoc_browser:latest
=end code
=end numitem
=numitem Set a browser's URL to C<localhost:3000>
=numitem Use the Editor as described in the Introduction
=begin numitem
End the container (using the id after C<--name> in the run command)
=code
podman stop rakedit
=end numitem

=place semantic:AUTHOR :caption<Author>
=end rakudoc